<main>
  <h1>Innopolis Museum of Natural History</h1>
  <p>Welcome to a small museum with a big collection. We look after more than 12,400 objects, from river shells to a complete mammoth skeleton.</p>
  <img src="/files/hero-mammoth.jpg" alt="The mammoth skeleton at night">
  <p><a href="/halls/rivers">Featured this month: the Volga Rivers hall</a>. It reopened after a long renovation and now has a sturgeon tank.</p>
  <p><a href="/about/?utm_source=home&amp;utm_medium=banner">About the museum</a> · <a href="#visit">Plan a visit</a> · <a href="/search?q=mammoth">Search the collection</a></p>
  <p><a href="javascript:void(0)">Open the map</a> or <a href="tel:+78435550199">call us</a> if you need directions.</p>
  <p>School computers can use our <a href="http://LocalHost:8765/about/">mirror site</a>. If you are in a hurry, <a href="HTTP://127.0.0.1:8765/halls/ice-age#skeleton">see the skeleton</a> first.</p>
  <p>We work with the <a href="http://127.0.0.1:8766/">Kazan Science Archive</a> on field research. Check the <a href="  /events/  ">  events page  </a> for lectures.</p>
  <p id="visit">Opening hours: Tuesday to Sunday, 10:00 to 18:00. The museum is closed on Mondays.</p>
</main>
